title: 'Google, "The Standard of Code Review" (eng-practices): approve a change once it clearly improves the code''s health, even if it is not perfect.'
pid: af788b42-fd06-4123-ad64-d7552d94be32
body: |2-
  https://google.github.io/eng-practices/review/reviewer/standard.html
  Read. "There is no such thing as 'perfect' code—there is only better
  code." Minor points are prefixed "Nit:" and are optional. A reviewer
  may still refuse a change nobody wants. Took: review for what makes
  the code worse or departs from what was asked, not for polish.
